\fs32\b Transcribing\b0\fs20\par
\par
Transcribing is the process of entering the information shown on a FreeBMD index scan into the WinBMD2 transcription grid.\par
\par
\fs24\b Entering an entry\b0\fs20\par
Enter each item from the scan into the corresponding field in the grid.\par
\par
The fields available depend on the type and date of the index being transcribed. WinBMD2 uses the batch information to determine which fields are required.\par
\par
\fs24\b Moving between fields\b0\fs20\par
Use Tab or Enter to move to the next field.\par
\par
When you reach the final field of an entry, WinBMD2 moves to the next entry so that transcription can continue without using the mouse.\par
\par
Shift+Tab moves back to the previous field.\par
\par
See The Grid topic for more information about grid navigation and entry behaviour.\par
\par
\fs24\b Copying repeated information\b0\fs20\par
Some information is frequently repeated from one entry to the next. WinBMD2 can automatically copy suitable values from the previous entry where appropriate, reducing the amount of typing required.\par
\par
Always compare copied information with the scan before continuing.\par
\par
\fs24\b Picklists and automatic completion\b0\fs20\par
WinBMD2 provides picklists for fields such as forenames and registration districts.\par
\par
As characters are entered, suitable values may be offered for selection. This can reduce typing and help maintain consistent spelling.\par
\par
Picklist behaviour can be changed in Options.\par
\par
\fs24\b Validation\b0\fs20\par
WinBMD2 checks entered values and warns when information appears unusual or does not match the expected format.\par
\par
A warning does not necessarily mean that the original index is wrong. The scan should always be treated as the source when deciding what should be transcribed.\par
\par
\fs24\b Special characters\b0\fs20\par
Names and other fields may occasionally contain characters that are difficult to enter directly from the keyboard.\par
\par
WinBMD2 provides a special-character selector for these cases.\par
\par
\fs24\b Working from the scan\b0\fs20\par
Keep the ScanView window positioned so that the entry being transcribed can be compared easily with the grid.\par
\par
The scan can be zoomed, moved and rotated as necessary. See the Scans topic for more information.\par
\par
\fs24\b Completing the transcription\b0\fs20\par
Continue entering each index entry until the required page or batch has been completed.\par
\par
The transcription should then be verified against the scan before it is uploaded to FreeBMD.\par
\par
See the Verification topic for details of the verification process.\par
